; The game's own copyrighted sounds: what does not play while the streamer mode (snd_streamer_mode)
; is on. The list is the game author's to keep; a module says the same of its own sounds in their
; descriptions and tracks (docs/dead-air/RADIO.md).
;
; [copyrighted], one line per sound:
;   <name>                 a sound name: its path under sounds, without the extension
;   <mask>                 the same with *, any run of characters (music\radio\*)
;   <name or mask> = <replacement>
;                          a sound that is not copyrighted, played in its place while the mode is on;
;                          a bare line has none, and the sound is simply not played
; Case and the direction of the slashes do not matter. A module's #file patch of this file adds to it.
;
; What is here, and why:
;   music\radio\*          the radio's music (play_radio_dar2), commercial recordings by the game
;                          author's word
;   radio\01\*             the level radios' music (common_radio): the same 45 recordings as
;                          music\radio\music_<n>, byte for byte
;   radio\<artist_title>   named after their performers and titles: Eduard Artemyev's "Meditation",
;                          FireLake's "Dirge for the Planet", "Razom nas bahato", Vulgargrad's "Alkogolik"

[copyrighted]
music\radio\*
radio\01\*
radio\edward_artemiev_meditation
radio\firelake_dirge_the_planet
radio\razom_nas_bahato
radio\vulgargrad_alkoholik
